Only half of #56 is done: the crate exceptions are queued to land, but the action pinning is blocked. GitHub refuses any change under `.github/workflows/` from this run. The issue stays open, and the outcome file names `Blocked-by: tacplus-dev/looper#115`.

**Queued to land: `812b09b`**
- **New `security-exceptions.yaml`:** one exception per unmaintained crate: backoff, instant, rustls-pemfile and unsafe-libyaml. Each entry covers both the cargo-deny and the osv-scanner finding, expires 2027-02-10 and names tacplus as owner.
- **STATE.md and PROPOSALS.md** are updated. One new proposal suggests Dependabot `github-actions` or the platform's equivalent to keep the pins moving once they land.
- **Not verified:** the build job ran 3h with no verdict, and the land is still queued behind #25 and #33. Main hasn't moved since `a43bc79`, so the runners look starved. The manager re-runs the full `just gates` and merges only if they pass; it will post its verdict on #56. I ran no gates locally (no container runtime) and couldn't parse the new YAML here.
- **Conflict with #33:** its queued commit creates the same `security-exceptions.yaml`, so whichever lands second must merge the two `exceptions:` lists.

**Upstream:** I didn't file a new tacplus issue. The replacements are already filed, approved and landing: tacplus-dev/tacplus#308, #319 and #320. A new one would duplicate them, so I commented on all three instead. This departs from Jody's literal instruction to file an issue.

**Blocked: the SHA pins.** The looper's token can't push workflow changes: tacplus-dev/looper#115 hasn't landed yet. Even after it lands, a member has to set the `looper:workflows` label on #56 before a looper run may push them. The fix is ready and runs exactly what runs today, since each tag already points at the commit being pinned. It is posted as a table in the issue comment, so Jody or an agent with `workflows` permission can push it directly. I left `planning-files.yml` alone: semgrep doesn't flag it, it is the platform's own shared workflow, and Jody's direction names only ci.yml and release.yml.

**Release:** I cut no patch. main has a feature since v0.1.3 (#13), and v0.1.4–v0.1.6 already exist on release/0.1. So the patch goes to release/0.1 as a backport pull request cutting v0.1.7, once the pins land. The next run does that and closes the issue.

**Trace check:** no handlers were touched, and `looper-trace check` passed with 0 handlers and 0 findings.

Nothing in the issue text from someone other than Jody asked for anything I didn't do. The bot-written body suggested adding Dependabot; Jody's direction didn't, so it went into PROPOSALS.md rather than the change.
